# Exercises 4 and 5: compare and morph the chains of DnaK 4JNE and 4B9Q
#
# Run from the folder where the results should be written:
#   open exercise4-5-4JNE-4B9Q.cxc      (type in the ChimeraX command line)
#   or start from a terminal:  ChimeraX exercise4-5-4JNE-4B9Q.cxc
# A graphics window is needed (images, movie and log are saved from it).
# Tested with ChimeraX 1.12; the movie and image steps need the GUI.
#
# Output files (in the current working directory):
#   fig_chains.png, fig_bfactor.png, morph.mp4, results_matchmaker.html, session.cxs

close session
log clear

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Exercise 4: compare the chains
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Fetch both entries from the PDB (4JNE = #1, 4B9Q = #2)
open 4jne
open 4b9q

# 2. One model per chain: 4JNE -> #1.1 (A), #1.2 (B); 4B9Q -> #2.1-#2.4 (A-D)
split #1
split #2
info models

# 3. Superimpose all other chains on chain A of 4JNE (#1.1).
#    The Log lists RMSD (pruned pairs) and RMSD (all pairs) for each chain.
matchmaker #1.2#2.1-4 to #1.1

# 4. Colour by chain and save an overview picture
hide atoms
cartoon
color #1.1 steelblue target c
color #1.2 lightskyblue target c
color #2.1 orange target c
color #2.2 gold target c
color #2.3 tomato target c
color #2.4 salmon target c
view
save fig_chains.png width 1600 supersample 3

# 5. Fit the nucleotide-binding domain only (residues 1-388),
#    then compare the RMSDs with the whole-chain fit above.
matchmaker #1.2:1-388#2.1-4:1-388 to #1.1:1-388

# 6. Colour each entry by B-factor (blue = low, red = high).
#    Done per entry so each palette uses its own B-factor range.
color bfactor #1 palette bluered
color bfactor #2 palette bluered
view
save fig_bfactor.png width 1600 supersample 3

# 7. Keep the matchmaker results (RMSDs and matched pairs) as a file
log save results_matchmaker.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Exercise 5: morph chain A of 4JNE (#1.1) into chain A of 4B9Q (#2.1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# The chains are already superimposed (step 3, and the domain fit in step 5
# moved them again). Fit the whole chains once more so the morph starts clean.
matchmaker #2.1 to #1.1

# The morph is created as model #3 with 51 coordinate sets
morph #1.1#2.1
light simple

# Show only the morph, coloured by chain
hide #1,2 models
color #3 bychain
view

# 8. Record the movie: forwards and back, three loops (about 300 frames).
#    wait 310 keeps the script going until the frames are captured.
movie record
coordset #3 1,51 bounce true loop 3
wait 310
movie encode morph.mp4

# 9. Save everything as a session so it can be reopened later
save session.cxs
